NAME
     awk - a pattern-and-action language for text

SYNOPSIS
     awk [-F SEP] [-v NAME=VALUE] 'PROGRAM' [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     awk runs PROGRAM against each line of its input. A program is a list
     of pattern { action } rules; a line is split into $1, $2 and so on,
     with $0 the whole of it and NF the number of fields. BEGIN and END
     rules run before and after everything else. The usual built-ins are
     here: NR, FNR, FS, OFS, NF, FILENAME, length, substr, index, split,
     sub, gsub, match, sprintf, printf, getline, and arithmetic with
     arrays and functions.

OPTIONS
     -F SEP           the field separator
     -v NAME=VALUE    set a variable before the program runs

EXAMPLES
     awk '{ s += $2 } END { print s }' sizes
     awk -F: '$3 >= 1000 { print $1 }' /etc/passwd

SEE ALSO
     sed(1), grep(1), bc(1)
